// The Drinking upgrade's recipes in a real crafting table, and the upgrade in a Sophisticated Storage
// chest. Only nodes that set deps.sophisticated_core have them on the runClient classpath, and
// deps.sophisticated_storage puts Sophisticated Storage there too.
//
// The player stands on a stone floor with a crafting table in front, and every ingredient is moved
// into the grid with the same slot clicks a screen sends, then the result is shift-clicked out.
// - craftBackpack, a waterskin, two glass bottles, Sophisticated Backpacks' upgrade base and an ender
//   pearl: the clear finds one Drinking upgrade.
// - craftStorage, the same around Sophisticated Storage's upgrade base: one Drinking upgrade.
// - craftAdvanced, a Drinking upgrade set to Dirty water, a diamond, two gold and three redstone: one
//   Advanced Drinking upgrade that still carries drink_min_purity 0.
// Then a Sophisticated Storage chest with two clean bottles takes the place of the table. The Drinking
// upgrade is shift-clicked in from the player's inventory; Sophisticated puts it in an upgrade slot
// only if the slot accepts it, which it does by the sophisticatedstorage:upgrade tag, and in the chest's
// own inventory otherwise. Upgrade slots are not among the menu's slots, so "storageMoved" shows the
// upgrade gone from both inventories. From thirst 4, standing next to the closed chest,
// "storageDrunk" shows 16 (a placed storage serves players within three blocks), and "storageAfter"
// two glass bottles in place of the water.
//
// SophisticatedAgent is a throwaway world: copy level.dat out of any 1.21.1 world into
// run/1.21.1-neoforge/saves/SophisticatedAgent, and tools/agent/integrations/sophisticated/sophisticated-pack into its datapacks
// folder, fresh for each run. Then:
//     ./gradlew ":1.21.1-neoforge:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/sophisticated/sophisticated-drinking-craft.jsonl -Pquickplay=SophisticatedAgent

